$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6,7-Dichloro-2,3-dihydro-1,4-benzodioxin (2). In a 30-gal reactor was
created a slurry of N-chlorosuccinimide (53.25 kg, 399 mol) in acetic
acid (63.6 kg). Into a 50-gal reactor, the N-chlorosuccinimide slurry was
added over 2 h to 2,3-dihydro-1,4-benzodioxin (1) (24.95 kg, 183 mol),
keeping the temperature between 70 and 100 °C. A rinse of the slurry
reactor and lines into the reaction with acetic acid (2 X 10 kg) was
done. After complete addition, the reaction was aged 30 min at 90-100 °C.
To the reaction mixture was added water (15.7 kg). The mixture was cooled
to 20 °C and aged overnight. The resulting crystals were filtered off,
washed with methanol (17.8 kg) and water (13 kg), and dried at 60-65 °C
to give 2. Yield 28.11 kg (75%), white solid. mp 151.2-151.6 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 4.24 (s, 4), 6.96 (s, 2); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 64.24 (CH2), 118.50
(CH), 123.97 (C), 142.78 (C). Anal. Calcd for C8H6Cl2O2:C, 46.86; H,
2.95. Found: C, 46.82; H, 2.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Process Development of the Synthetic Route to Sulamserod Hydrochloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kowalczyk, Bruce A.; Robinson, James III; Gardner, John O.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2001), 5(2), 116-121

