$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of indole and azaindole substrates. N-methyl-7-azaindole (1.0
g, 1.0 equiv.) and 3 (0.10 equiv.) was added to a 250 mL round bottom
flask followed by the addition of dichloromethane (0.10 M in indole).
N-chlorosuccinimide (1.2 equiv.) was added to the stirring reaction
mixture at room temperature, and the reaction was followed by TLC. Upon
completion, solvent was evaporated by rotovap, and the crude solid was
washed in ethyl acetate (100 mL) with brine (40 mL) 3 times. The organic
layer was dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and evaporated by rotovap
to yield a crude oil. The crude oil was purified by FCC (97:3
hexanes:ethyl acetate). 3-chloro-1-methyl-7-azaindole. 74% isolated yield
as an orange oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.37 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 1H),
7.691 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (s, 1H), 7.12 (dd, J = 7.9 Hz, 4.7 Hz,
1H), 3.86 (s, 3H); 13C (101 MHz, CDCl3) 146.50, 144.14, 126.78, 125.57,
118.50, 116.13, 103.20, 31.34; MS (ESI): Calculated C8H8ClN2 + [M+H]
167.0371. Found: 167.0371 m/z.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
