$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Heterocycles Standard
Procedure: To a solution of heterocycle (0.1 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) in
chloroform (1.0 mL) at r.t. was added chlorinating reagent (CBMG or NCS,
0.12 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) with stirring. The reaction was monitored by thin
layer chromatography until completion. For substrates, which do not go to
completion in 12 hrs, acetonitrile was employed as the solvent. Upon
consumption of starting material, the reaction was concentrated and
directly purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
4-chloro-1-((2-chlorophenyl)diphenylmethyl)-1H-imidazole (11). Procedure:
Standard procedure was followed using 1.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform.
tert-butyl 3-chloro-1H-indole-1-carboxylate (23). Standard procedure was
followed using 2.2 equiv. of CBMG in acetonitrile at 50 °C 1 hr. 23 in
73% yield as a white solid. It is of note that the R f of desired product
co-spots with the starting material and could only be distinguished by
anisaldehyde3 stain (picture of TLC shown below for clarity). m.p.: 51-54
°C; R f = 0.70 (10% ethyl acetate/hexanes). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
8.15 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.59 (m, 2H), 7.42-7.34 (m, 1H), 7.34-7.28 (m,
1H), 1.67 (s, 9H) ppm; 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.2, 134.6, 128.2,
125.6, 123.3, 122.3, 118.7, 115.5, 112.2, 84.4, 28.3 ppm; IR (neat) ν =
2978, 1733, 1368, 1448, 1246, 1148, 1056, 740 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calc’d
for C13H15ClNO2 + [M+H] 252.0786; found 252.0792.
