$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Chlorination of Heterocycles Standard Procedure: To a solution of
heterocycle (0.1 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) in chloroform (1.0 mL) at r.t. was
added chlorinating reagent (CBMG or NCS, 0.12 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) with
stirring. The reaction was monitored by thin layer chromatography until
completion. For substrates, which do not go to completion in 12 hrs,
acetonitrile was employed as the solvent. Upon consumption of starting
material, the reaction was concentrated and directly purified by column
chromatography on silica gel.
4-chloro-1-((2-chlorophenyl)diphenylmethyl)-1H-imidazole (11). Procedure:
Standard procedure was followed using 1.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform.
11 in 72% yield as a white solid. m.p.: 163-164 °C; R f = 0.70 (50% ethyl
acetate/hexanes); 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.54-7.49 (m, 1H), 7.47-7.40
(m, 7H), 7.38-7.36 (m, 2H), 7.29-7.23 (m, 3H), 7.02 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.3 Hz,
1H), 6.73 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H) ppm; 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 140.3,
139.8, 137.7, 135.7, 132.5, 130.5, 130.2, 129.3, 128.6, 128.3, 127.3,
117.5, 76.0 ppm; IR (neat) ν = 3061, 1445, 1225, 908, 730 cm-1; HRMS
(ESI-TOF) calc’d for C22H17Cl2N2 + [M+H] 379.0763; found 379.0767.
