$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4-Halo-3, 5-diarylisoxazoles 2-4; General
Procedure A solution of the isoxazole 1a-e (0.5-1.5 mmol) and the
N-halosuccinimide (1.1 equiv of NBS or NCS, or 1.5 equiv of NIS) in HOAc
(5 mL/mmol of isoxazole) was heated at gentle reflux (open condenser)
with the reaction progress followed by TLC (EtOAc-hexanes). If
halogenation was judged to no longer be proceeding, additional NXS was
added in increments until starting material was consumed (total NXS and
reaction times given in Table 1). With some substrates, halogenation
remained sluggish with addition of excess NXS, and thus the reaction
sequence was repeated using a strong acid catalyst. Once halogenation was
complete, the solution was diluted with H2O (or aqueous Na2S2O3 solution
in the case of iodination), and the resulting precipitate was collected,
washed with water, and recrystallized from EtOH or EtOH-H2O. Yields and
analytical data are given in Table 1 and Table 2. As noted in Table 1,
iodination of 1b was performed at r.t. To minimize decomposition of NIS,
all iodination reactions were protected from light by aluminum foil.
Product: 3e, Equiv NXS: 3, Added Acid: H2SO4, Reaction Time (h): 10,
Yield: (70%). Mp: 122-122.5 (°C). IR (KBr) cm-1: 3060, 1601, 1446, 1414,
1328, 1172, 1108, 845, 771, 708, 1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ, J(Hz): 7.59-7.61 (m,
3 H), 7.82-7.84 (m, 2 H), 7.99 (d, J= 8.3, 2 H), 8.22 (d, J= 8.2, 2 H),
13C NMR (DMSO-d6) δ: 105.8, 121.9, 125.5, 126.2, 126.2, 126.3, 126.3,
127.1, 128.0, 129.1, 130.5, 130.8, 131.0, 160.5, 162.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Convenient and improved halogenation of 3,5-diarylisoxazoles using
N-halosuccinimides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Day, Ruth Ann; Blake, Jacqueline A.; Stephens, Chad E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2003), (10), 1586-1590

