$DATUM 2-Bromo-3-(2-naphthylthio)anthra[2,3-b]thiophene (9b). To a solution of
9a (500 mg, 1.5 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was added nbutyllithium (1.63 M in
hexane, 1.2 mL, 2.0 mmol) at 0 °C. The mixture was warmed to rt and then
stirred for 1 h. 1,2-Dibromo-1,1,2,2-tetrachloroethane (645 mg, 2.0 mmol)
was then added to the mixture at 0 °C, and the resulting mixture was
stirred for 10 h at rt, and poured into a mixture of hydrochloric acid (1
M, 10 mL) and ethanol (50 mL), and a precipitate solid was collected by
filtration and washed with ethanol and hexane. The crude product was
purified by recrystallization from chlorofrom. 9b as a yellow solid (502
mg, 70%). Mp. 245-246 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz) δ 7.31 (dd, J = 1.9, 8.6 Hz,
1H), 7.37-7.46 (m, 4H), 7.64-7.68 (m, 2H), 7,69 (d, J = 8.7, 1H), 7.74
(dd, J = 1.7, 7.1, 1H), 7.95 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 8.00 (d, 7.9 Hz, 1H),
8.44 (s, 1H), 8.50 (s, 2H), 8.52 (s, 1H); EI-MS (70 eV) m/z = 470 (M+);
HRMS (APCI) m/z calcd for C26H16BrS2 [M + H]+: 470.98713 Found:
470.98724.
