$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R)-1-phenyl-N-((4-phenyl-1,3-oxazol-2-yl)methyl)ethanamine (5). To a
solution of 2-methyl-4-phenyloxazole 7 (0.40 g, 2.5 mmol) in CCl4 (10 mL)
was added N-chlorosuccinimide (0.73 g, 5.5 mmol) The reaction mixture was
heated to reflux for 2 h and acetic acid (0.75 mL, 13 mmol) was added and
reflux was continued. After 2 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with
diethyl ether and the organic phase was washed with 1 M NaOH (×1), brine
(×1), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated. Purification by flash
column chromatography on silica gel (5% to 10% ethyl acetate in hexanes)
gave 5-chloro-2-methyl-4-phenyloxazole (0.34 g, 70% yield) as a colorless
oil. 5-chloro-2-methyl-4-phenyloxazole, yield 0.34 g, 70% 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.89 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.43 (t, J = 7. 3 Hz, 2H), 7.33
(t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (s, 3H). MS (ESI, pos. ion) m/z: 194.1 (M + H).
HPLC: Retention time = 7.11 min (Method 2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
