$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 5-amino-2-chloro-4-methylbenzoic
acid 2. To a solution of 1 (3.02 g, 20 mmol) in DMF (30 ml) was added the
NCS (2.8 g, 21 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 1 h at 100 °C,
cooled to room temperature, left to stand overnight, and then slowly
poured into ice-water (100 ml) to precipitate a white solid. The solid
was filtered and dried to obtain compound.
4-amino-3-chloro-5-methylbenzoic acid 7a. 69.6 % yield, white solid. m.p.
>197 °C (decomposition). 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6) δ: 2.18 (s, 3H, CH3), 5.75
(s, 2H, NH2), 7.55 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 7.77 (s, 1H, Ar-H), 12.37 (br. s, 1H,
COOH).
