$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step A: methyl 4-bromo-1H-imidazole-5-carboxylate. N-bromosuccinimide
(0.900 g, 5.0 mmol) was added to a stirred solution of methyl
1H-imidazole-4-carboxylate (0.630 g, 5.0 mmol) in CH3CN (50 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred for 12 hours in the dark and then
concentrated in the presence of silica gel. The absorbed crude material
was purified by column chromatography (20-100% EtOAc/hexanes) to afford
the title compound. White solid, yield (0.708 g, 70%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ ppm 11.00 (br. s., 1 H), 7.81 (s, 1 H), 3.81 (s, 3 H).
ES-LCMS: m/z 204.9, 206.9 (M+1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rational Design of Potent Non-Nucleoside Inhibitors of HIV-1 Reverse
Transcriptase
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
