$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Heterocycles Standard
Procedure: To a solution of heterocycle (0.1 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) in
chloroform (1.0 mL) at r.t. was added chlorinating reagent (CBMG or NCS,
0.12 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) with stirring. The reaction was monitored by thin
layer chromatography until completion. For substrates, which do not go to
completion in 12 hrs, acetonitrile was employed as the solvent. Upon
consumption of starting material, the reaction was concentrated and
directly purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
4-chloro-1-((2-chlorophenyl)diphenylmethyl)-1H-imidazole (11). Procedure:
Standard procedure was followed using 1.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform.
3-chloro-1-methyl-1H-indole-2-carbaldehyde (21). Standard procedure was
followed using 1.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform for 30 min. 21 in 70%
yield as a white solid. m.p.: 80-82 °C; R f = 0.50 (15% ethyl
ether/hexanes); 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.18 (s, 1H), 7.74 (d, J = 8.2
Hz, 1H), 7.50-7.43 (m, 1H), 7.38 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (d, J = 7.2
Hz, 1H), 4.07 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 181.4, 138.8,
129.2, 128.2, 124.4, 121.6, 120.7, 119.4, 110.6, 32.0 ppm; IR (neat) ν =
2928, 1667, 1470, 1188, 739 cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calc’d for C10H9ClNO+
[M+H] 194.0367; found 194.0369.
