$DATUM 15799-89-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Halogenation. BF3-H2O (4
mL) was added to a mixture of the deactivated aromatic compound (10 mmol)
and N-halosuccinimide (10 mmol) in a 30 mL Nalgene bottle. The bottle was
closed, and the mixture was stirred at the required temperature (room
temperature for most reactions) for the specified period of time (Tables
1-3). For higher temperature reactions, pressure tubes were used. The
progress of the reactions was monitored by GC/MS analysis. The reaction
mixture was then completely transferred to a separatory funnel using
water (30 mL) and dichloromethane (2 x 30 mL) and thoroughly shaken to
extract the product into the organic layer. The organic layer was washed
with saturated solution of sodium bisulfite or sodium thiosulfate (15 mL)
to remove any free halogen present followed by saturated sodium
bicarbonate solution (30 mL) and brine (30 mL). It was then washed with
water (2 x 30 mL) and dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate. The solvent
was removed under reduced pressure, and the product was purified by
fractional distillation or recrystallization from petroleum ether.
compound-4c. yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Halosuccinimide/BF3-H2O, Efficient Electrophilic Halogenating Systems
for Aromatics
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
