$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Electrophilic
Aromatic Halogenation; 4-Bromo-2-chloro-1-methoxybenzene (2a-Cl) and
2,4-Dichloro-1-methoxybenzene (2a-diCl; Ref 20): To a solution of
4-bromoanisole (1a; 200.8 mg, 1.09 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in MeCN (2 mL) was
added Nchlorosuccinimide (NCS; 158.3 mg, 1.19 mmol, 1.1 equiv) at r.t. to
give a slightly cloudy mixture. Chlorotrimethylsilane (TMSCl; 14 μL, 0.11
mmol, 0.1 equiv) was then added dropwise to the reaction mixture. Within
a few minutes, the reaction mixture became clear pale yellow solution.
The mixture was stirred continuously at r.t. for 1 h and H2O was added to
it. The separated aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic phases were washed with sat. aq NaCl, dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated. The crude material was purified by flash SiO2 column eluted
with 5-10% EtOAc-hexane. 5-bromobenzo[d][1,3]dioxole (2k-Br): Yield 181.0
mg of product mixture (76% of 2k-Br, 16% of 2k-diBr, based on NMR ratio
2k-Br: 2k-diBr = 4.8: 1.0; as a colorless oil). IR (neat): νmax 2896,
1500, 1469, 1228 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.05 (s, 0.44H, 2k-diBr
minor), 6.94-6.91 (m, 2H), 6.67 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 5.98 (s, 0.48H,
2k-diBr minor), 5.95 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 148.5, 147.9
(2k-diBr minor), 146.9, 124.3, 115.3 (2k-diBr minor), 113.1, 112.2,
109.5, 102.3 (2k-diBr minor), 101.6. APCI-HRMS calcd for C7H5BrO2 (Br-79)
(M)+• 199.9467, found 199.9464.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, in-situ generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Practical and metal-free electrophilic aromatic halogenation by
inter-halogen compounds generated in situ from N-halosuccinimide and
catalytic TMSCl
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Maibunkaew, Tapanee; Thongsornkleeb, Charnsak; Tummatorn, Jumreang;
Bunrit, Anon; Ruchirawat, Somsak
