$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure11 To a solution
of NBS (10.0 mmol, 1.78 g) in CH2Cl2 (80.0 mL) cooled to -78 °C was added
ZrCl4 (0.5 mmol, 116.5 mg), followed by anisole (10.0 mmol, 1.10 mL)
under nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction was stirred for 5 h and then
quenched by sat. NaHCO3 aq solution. The extracted organic phase (CH2Cl2)
was washed with brine and dried over NaSO4. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure to give as sole product. No further purification is
necessary. Yield 93%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, optimized on reaction conditions,catalyst, conversion is
93%
